0+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxPN1VZVUJVZGZyeG1qeVRscTVtRkdGYmNyNFRWR01YUVJ4djRBMHhFbTAwLWdXU0xxU2xad2NQdk9QUVQta3g2bGhsLXFZWTBJTGc2a3BHbV9taUVPOW9GTEdVWFlwQ3pkeGxmR1pFQ1k3VEh3M3k3OEFjRU5ZVHpKT01DbzBIcThHRFY5bg?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 8.2, "prior_sd": 5.0, "poll_margin": 6.92, "poll_sd": 5.16, "poll_weight": 0.48, "fundamentals": {"margin": 10.3, "lean": 2.0, "environment": 7.74, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 0.56}, "rating_margin": 6.79, "sigma_race": 4.5, "sigma_total": 5.14, "baseline_margin": 7.58, "analyst_adjustment": -0.58, "key_factors": ["Consistent polling lead for Pappas across pollsters of both leanings", "Pappas's large fundraising edge over Sununu", "Sununu's brand and outside spending keep the race from being Safe D", "Open seat with no incumbent on the ballot"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Pappas ahead by 5 to 7 points, including Republican-leaning pollsters, and prediction markets price his win chances above 90 percent. Sununu's name recognition and heavier outside support argue for some tightening, but the evidence points to a clear Democratic advantage.", "watch": "A late shift among independents toward Sununu, or a national Republican wave environment, could narrow the margin in the final days.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jeanne Shaheen (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's open Senate seat pits Representative Chris Pappas against former Senator John Sununu, with Shaheen retiring. Pappas has led in every poll since mid-September, with margins of five to seven points across pollsters of varying leanings, and averages put the race near seven points Democratic. Pappas has also raised far more money than Sununu, though outside groups have spent more on Sununu's behalf. Prediction markets give Pappas roughly a 93 percent chance of winning.\n\nRaters mostly call the race Lean or Likely Democratic, with none placing it in Republican territory. Sununu has c